        '[KAS: Prelims-P1, Mains-GS1] [UPSC: Prelims-GS1, Mains-GS1]', 'Distinctive medieval Hoysala temple style (11th–14th century) constructed using fine-grained chloritic schist (soapstone): Stellate (star-shaped) ground plan raised on a high platform (Jagati), richly carved friezes of elephants, lions, horses, and floral creepers; Celebrated temples: Chennakeshava Temple at Belur (sculpted Madanika/Shalabhanjika bracket figures), Hoysaleshwara Temple at Halebidu (twin Dvikuta shrine with 240+ relief statues), and Keshava Temple at Somanathapura (complete Trikuta shrine); Inscribed on UNESCO World Heritage list in 2023.', ARRAY['Hoysala Architecture (UNESCO 2023)', 'Stellate / Star-shaped Ground Plan', 'Chloritic Schist / Soapstone Carving', 'Belur Chennakeshava Temple', 'Halebidu Hoysaleshwara Dvikuta', 'Somanathapura Keshava Trikuta', 'Madanika Bracket Sculptures']::text[], ARRAY['Hoysala', 'Architecture', 'Sculptures', 'UNESCO', 'World', 'Heritage', '2023', 'Distinctive', 'medieval', 'temple', 'style', '11th', '14th', 'century', 'constructed', 'using', 'fine', 'grained', 'chloritic', 'schist', 'soapstone', 'Stellate', 'star', 'shaped', 'ground', 'plan', 'raised', 'high', 'platform', 'Jagati', 'richly', 'carved', 'friezes', 'elephants', 'lions', 'horses', 'floral', 'creepers', 'Celebrated', 'temples', 'Chennakeshava', 'Temple', 'Belur', 'sculpted', 'Madanika', 'Shalabhanjika', 'bracket', 'figures', 'Hoysaleshwara', 'Halebidu', 'twin', 'Dvikuta', 'shrine', '240', 'relief', 'statues', 'Keshava', 'Somanathapura', 'complete', 'Trikuta', 'Inscribed', 'list', 'Star', 'Ground', 'Plan', 'Chloritic', 'Schist', 'Soapstone', 'Carving', 'Bracket']::text[],
