        '[KAS: Prelims-P1, Mains-GS1] [UPSC: Prelims-GS1, Mains-GS1]', 'Diverse architectural expressions in Karnataka: Kadamba dynasty''s stepped pyramidal Shikhara (Kadamba Shikhara, Halasi temples); Western Ganga dynasty''s Jain architectural legacy, climaxing in the monolithic 57-foot statue of Gommateshwara / Bahubali carved on Vindhyagiri hill at Shravanabelagola by Chavundaraya (981 CE, Mahamastakabhisheka festival); Adil Shahi dynasty of Bijapur featuring Gol Gumbaz (one of the largest single domes in the world with an acoustic Whispering Gallery) and Ibrahim Rauza.', ARRAY['Kadamba Stepped Shikhara', 'Gommateshwara Monolith Shravanabelagola', 'Chavundaraya Western Ganga Dynasty', 'Mahamastakabhisheka Festival', 'Gol Gumbaz Whispering Gallery', 'Ibrahim Rauza Bijapur']::text[], ARRAY['Kadamba', 'Ganga', 'Rashtrakuta', 'Deccan', 'Sultanate', 'Architecture', 'Diverse', 'architectural', 'expressions', 'Karnataka', 'dynasty', 'stepped', 'pyramidal', 'Shikhara', 'Halasi', 'temples', 'Western', 'Jain', 'legacy', 'climaxing', 'monolithic', '57', 'foot', 'statue', 'Gommateshwara', 'Bahubali', 'carved', 'Vindhyagiri', 'hill', 'Shravanabelagola', 'Chavundaraya', '981', 'CE', 'Mahamastakabhisheka', 'festival', 'Adil', 'Shahi', 'Bijapur', 'featuring', 'Gol', 'Gumbaz', 'one', 'largest', 'single', 'domes', 'world', 'acoustic', 'Whispering', 'Gallery', 'Ibrahim', 'Rauza', 'Stepped', 'Monolith', 'Dynasty', 'Festival']::text[],
