        '[UPSC: Prelims-GS1, Mains-GS1] [KAS: Prelims-P1, Mains-GS1] [SSC: GA]', 'Alfred Wegener''s Continental Drift Theory (1912): Supercontinent Pangaea surrounded by Panthalassa; Evidence: Jig-saw fit of South American and African Atlantic coastlines, matching ancient orogenic rock belts, fossil distribution of freshwater reptile Mesosaurus and seed fern Glossopteris, and Permo-Carboniferous glacial tillite beds across Gondwana fragments; Paleomagnetism and polar wandering curves confirming continental mobility.', ARRAY['Wegener''s Continental Drift Theory', 'Supercontinent Pangaea & Panthalassa', 'Jig-saw Coastline Matching', 'Glossopteris & Mesosaurus Fossil Evidence', 'Carboniferous Glacial Tillite', 'Paleomagnetism & Polar Wandering']::text[], ARRAY['Continental', 'Drift', 'Theory', 'Paleomagnetic', 'Evidence', 'Alfred', 'Wegener', '1912', 'Supercontinent', 'Pangaea', 'surrounded', 'Panthalassa', 'Jig', 'saw', 'fit', 'South', 'American', 'African', 'Atlantic', 'coastlines', 'matching', 'ancient', 'orogenic', 'rock', 'belts', 'fossil', 'distribution', 'freshwater', 'reptile', 'Mesosaurus', 'seed', 'fern', 'Glossopteris', 'Permo', 'Carboniferous', 'glacial', 'tillite', 'beds', 'across', 'Gondwana', 'fragments', 'Paleomagnetism', 'polar', 'wandering', 'curves', 'confirming', 'continental', 'mobility', 'Coastline', 'Matching', 'Fossil', 'Glacial', 'Tillite', 'Polar', 'Wandering']::text[],
