        'Subtopic_Entity', 'Geography & Earth Systems', 'geography_earth_systems', 'geography_earth_systems.oceanography_marine_systems.ocean_water_dynamics',
        ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY['geography_earth_systems', 'geography_earth_systems.oceanography_marine_systems', 'geography_earth_systems.oceanography_marine_systems.ocean_water_dynamics']::text[], '{"upsc": ["Prelims-GS1", "Mains-GS1"], "kas": ["Prelims-P1", "Mains-GS1"], "ssc": ["GA"]}'::jsonb,
        '[UPSC: Prelims-GS1, Mains-GS1] [KAS: Prelims-P1, Mains-GS1] [SSC: GA]', 'Tide generating forces: Differential gravitational attraction of Moon (dominant 2.17x greater) and Sun, balanced by centrifugal force creating two tidal bulges on opposite sides of Earth; Astronomical tidal cycles: Spring Tides (Syzygy alignment: Conjunction/New Moon and Opposition/Full Moon when lunar and solar gravitational forces reinforce each other producing highest tidal range); Neap Tides (Quadrature alignment: First and Third Quarter moons when Sun and Moon act at right angles producing lowest tidal range); Diurnal (one high, one low daily), Semidiurnal (two equal highs, two equal lows daily), Mixed tides; Tidal bore phenomena (steep turbulent wall of water rushing up shallow estuaries, Hooghly River, Qiantang River China, Bay of Fundy world''s highest tides 16m); Amphidromic points (cotidal nodal points where tidal range is zero).', ARRAY['Tidal Bulges (Moon & Sun Gravitational Forces)', 'Spring Tides (Syzygy Alignment)', 'Neap Tides (Quadrature 90 deg)', 'Semidiurnal & Diurnal Tides', 'Tidal Bore (Hooghly River)', 'Bay of Fundy Extreme Tidal Range (16m)', 'Amphidromic Nodal Points']::text[], ARRAY['Tides', 'Gravitational', 'Forces', 'Syzygy', 'Quadrature', 'Tidal', 'Bores', 'Tide', 'generating', 'forces', 'Differential', 'gravitational', 'attraction', 'Moon', 'dominant', '17x', 'greater', 'Sun', 'balanced', 'centrifugal', 'force', 'creating', 'two', 'tidal', 'bulges', 'opposite', 'sides', 'Earth', 'Astronomical', 'cycles', 'Spring', 'alignment', 'Conjunction', 'New', 'Opposition', 'Full', 'when', 'lunar', 'solar', 'reinforce', 'each', 'other', 'producing', 'highest', 'range', 'Neap', 'First', 'Third', 'Quarter', 'moons', 'act', 'right', 'angles', 'lowest', 'Diurnal', 'one', 'high', 'low', 'daily', 'Semidiurnal', 'equal', 'highs', 'lows', 'Mixed', 'tides', 'bore', 'phenomena', 'steep', 'turbulent', 'wall', 'water', 'rushing', 'up', 'shallow', 'estuaries', 'Hooghly', 'River', '