        'geography_earth_systems.economic_resource_geography.location_factors_of_primary_secondary_tertiary_industries.industrial_location_theories_and_weberian_model', 'industrial_location_theories_and_weberian_model', 'Industrial Location Theories: Weberian Least Cost & Locational Factors', 4,
        'Subtopic_Entity', 'Geography & Earth Systems', 'geography_earth_systems', 'geography_earth_systems.economic_resource_geography.location_factors_of_primary_secondary_tertiary_industries',
        ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY['geography_earth_systems', 'geography_earth_systems.economic_resource_geography', 'geography_earth_systems.economic_resource_geography.location_factors_of_primary_secondary_tertiary_industries']::text[], '{"upsc": ["Prelims-GS1", "Mains-GS1"], "kas": ["Prelims-P1", "Mains-GS1"], "ssc": ["GA"]}'::jsonb,
        '[UPSC: Prelims-GS1, Mains-GS1] [KAS: Prelims-P1, Mains-GS1] [SSC: GA]', 'Theoretical models and economic geography of industrial siting: Alfred Weber''s Theory of Industrial Location / Least Cost Theory (Material Index = weight of localized raw material / weight of finished product; Gross / Weight-losing raw materials MI > 1 pulling industry to raw material source; Pure raw materials MI = 1 locating anywhere; Ubiquitous raw materials like air/water pulling towards market; Concept of Isotims lines of equal transport cost and Isodapanes lines of equal total transport costs, Critical Isodapane; Labour orientation and agglomeration economies); August Lösch''s Profit Maximization Theory and Walter Christaller''s Central Place Theory; Primary locational factors: Raw material proximity, energy/power availability, skilled/unskilled labour, transport networks, capital access, government industrial zoning, environmental clearances, and port proximity for export-oriented manufacturing.', ARRAY['Alfred Weber Least Cost Theory', 'Material Index (Weight-Losing vs Pure)', 'Isotims & Isodapanes (Critical Isodapane)', 'Agglomeration Economies', 'August Lösch Profit Maximization', 'Primary Industrial Locational Factors']::text[], ARRAY['Industrial', 'Location', 'Theories', 'Weberian', 'Least', 'Cost', 'Locational', 'Factors', 'Theoretical', 'models', 'economic', 'geography', 'industrial', 'siting', 'Alfred', 'Weber', 'Theory', 'Material', 'Index', 'weight', 'localized', 'raw', 'material', 'finished', 'product', 'Gross', 'Weight', 'losing', 'materials', 'MI', 'pulling', 'industry', 'source', 'Pure', 'locating', 'anywhere', 'Ubiquitous', 'like', 'air', 'water', 'towards', 'market', 'Concept', 'Isotims', 'lines', 'equal', 'transport', 'cost', 'Isodapanes', 'total', 'costs', 'Critical', 'Isodapane', 'Labour', 'orientation', 'agglomeration', 'economies', 'August', 'sch', 'Profit', 'Maximization', 'Walter', 'Christaller', 'Central', 'Place', 'Primary', 'locational', 'factors', 'Ra