    (
        'geography_earth_systems.economic_resource_geography.location_factors_of_primary_secondary_tertiary_industries.textile_chemical_and_agro_processing_industries', 'textile_chemical_and_agro_processing_industries', 'Textile, Chemical & Agro-Processing Industries: Cotton, Sugar & Jute', 4,
        'Subtopic_Entity', 'Geography & Earth Systems', 'geography_earth_systems', 'geography_earth_systems.economic_resource_geography.location_factors_of_primary_secondary_tertiary_industries',
        ARRAY[]::text[], ARRAY['geography_earth_systems', 'geography_earth_systems.economic_resource_geography', 'geography_earth_systems.economic_resource_geography.location_factors_of_primary_secondary_tertiary_industries']::text[], '{"upsc": ["Prelims-GS1", "Mains-GS1"], "kas": ["Prelims-P1", "Mains-GS1"], "ssc": ["GA"]}'::jsonb,
        '[UPSC: Prelims-GS1, Mains-GS1] [KAS: Prelims-P1, Mains-GS1] [SSC: GA]', 'Locational shifts and clustering of consumer and agro-based industries: Cotton Textile Industry (pure raw material, historically located in Mumbai and Ahmedabad due to humid maritime climate preventing yarn breakage, port facilities, and black soil hinterland; subsequent spatial decentralization to handloom/powerloom hubs in Coimbatore ''Manchester of South India'', Tirupur knitwear capital, Surat synthetic textiles, Ludhiana woolen knitwear); Jute Industry (highly localized in Hooghly river basin West Bengal due to proximity to raw jute cultivation in Ganga-Brahmaputra delta, abundant fresh water for retting, cheap labour from Bihar/Odisha, and Kolkata port); Sugar Industry (weight-losing, perishable raw material crushed within 24 hours of harvest; major locational shift from Northern India UP/Bihar to Southern and Western India Maharashtra/Karnataka/Tamil Nadu driven by tropical maritime climate, longer crushing season, higher sucrose content in cane, and thriving cooperative sugar mill structure); Chemical and Petrochemical complexes (concentrated near refineries and ports: Jamnagar refinery complex, Dahej PCPIR in Gujarat, Nagothane in Maharashtra).', ARRAY['Cotton Textile (Mumbai to Coimbatore & Tirupur)', 'Jute Retting & Hooghly River Basin', 'Sugar Industry Shift (North to Maharashtra)', 'Tropical vs Subtropical Cane Sucrose Content', 'Petrochemical Hubs (Jamnagar & Dahej PCPIR)', 'Agro-Processing Cooperatives']::text[], ARRAY['Textile', 'Chemical', 'Agro', 'Processing', 'Industries', 'Cotton', 'Sugar', 'Jute', 'Locational', 'shifts', 'clustering', 'consumer', 'agro', 'based', 'industries', 'Industry', 'pure', 'raw', 'material', 'historically', 'located', 'Mumbai', 'Ahmedabad', 'due', 'humid', 'maritime', 'climate', 'preventing', 'yarn', 'breakage', 'port', 'facilities', 'black', 'soil', 'hinterland', 'subsequent', 'spatial', 'decentralization', 'handloom', 'powerloom', 'hubs', 