        '[UPSC: Prelims-GS1, Mains-GS1] [KAS: Prelims-P1, Mains-GS1] [SSC: GA]', 'Physical architecture and northern environments of Canada: Canadian Shield / Laurentian Plateau (vast U-shaped region of exposed pre-Cambrian crystalline igneous and metamorphic rocks covering over half of Canada, heavily scoured by Pleistocene continental ice sheets; thousands of glacial lakes: Great Bear Lake, Great Slave Lake deepest in North America, Lake Athabasca, Reindeer Lake, Lake Winnipeg); St. Lawrence Lowlands and River (vital commercial waterway linking Great Lakes to the Atlantic Ocean via the St. Lawrence Seaway); Appalachian Region of the Maritime Provinces (Nova Scotia, New Brunswick, Newfoundland); Western Canadian Cordillera (Canadian Rockies, Coast Mountains, Mount Logan 5,959m highest peak in Canada located in Yukon); Arctic Archipelago and Tundra biome (permafrost, muskeg bogs, pingos, Beaufort Sea, Northwest Passage maritime route through high-latitude ice).', ARRAY['Canadian Shield (Laurentian Plateau)', 'Glacial Lakes (Great Bear & Great Slave Lakes)', 'St. Lawrence Seaway Maritime Corridor', 'Canadian Cordillera & Mount Logan', 'Arctic Archipelago & Permafrost Tundra', 'Northwest Passage Arctic Route']::text[], ARRAY['Canada', 'Canadian', 'Shield', 'Glacial', 'Drainage', 'Arctic', 'Tundra', 'Physical', 'architecture', 'northern', 'environments', 'Laurentian', 'Plateau', 'vast', 'shaped', 'region', 'exposed', 'pre', 'Cambrian', 'crystalline', 'igneous', 'metamorphic', 'rocks', 'covering', 'over', 'half', 'heavily', 'scoured', 'Pleistocene', 'continental', 'ice', 'sheets', 'thousands', 'glacial', 'lakes', 'Great', 'Bear', 'Lake', 'Slave', 'deepest', 'North', 'America', 'Athabasca', 'Reindeer', 'Winnipeg', 'St', 'Lawrence', 'Lowlands', 'River', 'vital', 'commercial', 'waterway', 'linking', 'Lakes', 'Atlantic', 'Ocean', 'via', 'Seaway', 'Appalachian', 'Region', 'Maritime', 'Provinces', 'Nova', 'Scotia', 'New', 'Brunswick', 'Newfoundland', 'Western', 'Cordillera', 